      "id": 1,
      "text": "Valley Center’s History Museum opened in 2003, preserving the town’s pioneer roots and local stories.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_Center%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Valley Center Art Association began in 1985, giving artists a long‑standing community gallery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hiddensandiego.com/things-to-do/places/valley-center-historical-society",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A taxidermy mount of a California grizzly, the state’s extinct icon, hangs in the historical society’s exhibit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hiddensandiego.com/things-to-do/places/valley-center-historical-society",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historical society also showcases a replica of one of the first airplanes built just six years after the Wright brothers’ flight.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hiddensandiego.com/things-to-do/places/valley-center-historical-society",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hollywood filmed classics like \"Mad, Mad World\" and \"Invaders from Mars\" right in Valley Center’s streets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hiddensandiego.com/things-to-do/places/valley-center-historical-society",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 1866, the largest grizzly ever recorded in California was shot in what is now Valley Center, a fact still remembered by locals.",
